  <x:String x:Key="Demo.Reader.Title">AKP202W Teaching Plan (demo).pdf</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Demo.Reader.Summary">A demo document the sandbox draws itself: the course description, how the marks are split, the weekly schedule, and the group project brief. Everything on screen comes from the reader's own page pipeline, so the layout you see is the layout the real file gets.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Demo.Reader.Section1">Course description and learning outcomes</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Demo.Reader.Section2">Assessment weights</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Demo.Reader.Section3">Weekly schedule, weeks 1–7</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Demo.Reader.Section4">Group project brief</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Demo.Reader.PageText">Demo page text. With a real file this is the PDF text layer of the page.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Demo.Reader.SelectionText">Demo selection. With a real file these are the words under the box.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Demo.Reader.DefaultQuestion">What does this mean, and why does it matter?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Demo.Reader.Answer">Sure — here is how I would read that part:

First, the sentence is defining the term before using it, so read it as a definition rather than an argument. Second, the example right after it is the one to remember: the exam usually asks you to apply the rule to a case like that, not to repeat the definition. I would underline the rule and jot the example beside it, because those two together are what the marking scheme rewards.</x:String>
  <!-- advanced settings: prompts and inference parameters (P0 read-only) -->
  <x:String x:Key="Advanced.Title">Advanced settings</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Advanced.Note">Every prompt this app sends and the parameters it sends them with. Segments marked "fixed by code" are what the parsers depend on; the rest can be edited, and the shipped text always stays available as Restore default.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Advanced.Footer">Edits are stored in state/prompts.json as overrides; the defaults stay in the code. Restarting the app keeps your edits, and Restore default brings the original back.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Advanced.Close">Close</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Advanced.CallSite">used by</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Advanced.Locked">fixed by code</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Advanced.Group.prompt">Prompt</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Advanced.Group.parameter">Parameter</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Advanced.Group.constant">Tuning constant</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Chat.Title">Main chat system prompt</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Chat.Purpose">Sent as the system message on every assistant turn; carries the tool catalogue and the JSON protocol.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Chat.Persona">Persona and rules</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Chat.Tools">Tool catalogue</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Chat.Protocol">Output protocol</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Summary.Title">One-line summary</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Summary.Purpose">Summarises a fetched item into the raw zone (R1) when a model is available.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Summary.Instruction">Instruction</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Judge.Title">Relevance judge</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Judge.Purpose">Decides whether unconfirmed material relates to the question; returns a verdict and a handle, never the text.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Judge.Rule">Rule</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Judge.Format">Output rule</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.JudgeFormat.Title">Judge reply format</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.JudgeFormat.Purpose">Appended to the judge's user message — this is the JSON array the parser reads.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.JudgeFormat.Instruction">Format</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Privacy.Title">Privacy check (outbound gate)</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Privacy.Purpose">Runs before anything leaves the machine. Locked: weakening it would weaken the gate itself.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Privacy.System">System instruction</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.Privacy.Question">Question plus the text</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.LecturePersona.Title">Point read: persona</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.LecturePersona.Purpose">The senior-student voice for the outline pass and every question in the reader.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.LecturePersona.Persona">Persona</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.LectureOutline.Title">Point read: outline instruction</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.LectureOutline.Purpose">Appended to the whole-file corpus; asks for a summary and a page index.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.LectureOutline.Instruction">Instruction</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.LectureOutline.Format">Output contract</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.LectureVision.Title">Point read: describe a region</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.LectureVision.Purpose">Only when the selected box has no text layer (scanned page, chart, photo).</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.LectureVision.Instruction">Instruction</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.ChatTemplate.Title">Local chat template</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.ChatTemplate.Purpose">How the bundled GGUF expects the conversation to be wrapped. Tied to the model family.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Prompt.ChatTemplate.Template">Template</x:String>
